<div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center"
             style="cursor:pointer;" @onclick="Toggle">
            <h5 class="card-title mb-0">📖 How the Schengen 90/180 Rule Works</h5>
            <span>@(expanded ? "▲" : "▼")</span>
        </div>

        @if (expanded)
        {
            <hr />
            <div class="rules-content">
                <h6>The Basic Rule</h6>
                <p>
                    As a UK citizen travelling visa-free, you may spend a maximum of
                    <strong>90 days in any 180-day period</strong> within the Schengen Area.
                    This is <em>not</em> a fixed six-month block — it is a rolling window that
                    recalculates every day.
                </p>

                <h6>How the Rolling Window Works</h6>
                <p>
                    On any given day, the rule looks back exactly 180 days and counts every day
                    you were present in the Schengen Area during that window. If the total is
                    90 or fewer, you are within the limit.
                </p>
                <div class="rules-example">
                    <strong>Example:</strong> If today is 1 July 2025, the calculator counts all
                    days you spent in Schengen from 2 January 2025 to 1 July 2025. As each day
                    passes, old trip days drop off the back of the window and free up allowance.
                </div>

                <h6>Common Misconceptions</h6>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>It does not reset on 1 January.</strong> The window is always the 180 days before today.</li>
                    <li><strong>Both entry and exit days count.</strong> A trip from Mon to Fri is 5 days, not 3.</li>
                    <li><strong>It applies across all Schengen countries combined.</strong>
                        A week in Spain followed by a week in France is 14 days total, not 7.</li>
                    <li><strong>Exceeding 90 days is a serious offence</strong> — you may be denied entry,
                        fined, or banned from re-entry for a period.</li>
                </ul>

                <h6>Which Countries are in the Schengen Area?</h6>
                <p>
                    Austria, Belgium, Croatia, Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France,
                    Germany, Greece, Hungary, Iceland, Italy, Latvia, Liechtenstein, Lithuania,
                    Luxembourg, Malta, Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Slovakia, Slovenia,
                    Spain, Sweden, Switzerland.
                </p>
                <p class="mb-0">
                    <strong>Not in Schengen:</strong> Ireland, Cyprus, Bulgaria, Romania — and of
                    course the UK itself.
                </p>
            </div>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private bool expanded;
    private void Toggle() => expanded = !expanded;
}
